<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madeleine de La Tour d'Auvergne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1498–1519</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madeleine de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-la-tour-dauvergne">La Tour d'Auvergne</a> was a French noblewoman, heiress to the counties of Auvergne and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a>, who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorenzo-de-medici">Lorenzo de' Medici</a>, Duke of Urbino, in 1518. She died weeks after giving birth to their daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-de-medici">Catherine de' Medici</a>, later queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Through her, Catherine inherited the county of Auvergne, which eventually passed to the French crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madeleine-de-la-tour-dauvergne.jpg" alt="Madeleine de La Tour d'Auvergne" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Jean Perréal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_di_gentildonna_(Madeleine_de_la_Tour_d%27Auvergne_%3F)_-_Uffizi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
